<title>SINGAPORE: Hotel Properties places bond proceeds.</title>
<headline>Hotel Properties places bond proceeds.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hotel Properties Ltd said on Monday it had used about Singapore $80.8 million raised from the issue of bonds due in 2002 to repay bank borrowings.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that amoount of proceeds from the issue of S$100 million of unsecured fixed rate bonds was used to refinance loans of certain subsidiaries.</p>
<p>These loans included those for the construction of the Four Seasons Hotel in Singapore, investment in the Cuscaden Road property and HPL House, it said.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
